  "question": {
    "text": "Let $y=y(x)$ be the solution of the differential equation $\\left(x^2+4\\right)^2 d y+\\left(2 x^3 y+8 x y-2\\right) d x=0$. If $y(0)=0$, then $y(2)$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "n9j4G",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{32}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ir3Nj",
      "text": "${2}{\\pi}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KZLHj",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{8}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OeHjg",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{16}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{d y}{d x}+y\\left(\\frac{2 x^3+8 x}{\\left(x^2+4\\right)^2}\\right)=\\frac{2}{\\left(x^2+4\\right)^2} \\\\\n& \\frac{d y}{d x}+y\\left(\\frac{2 x}{x^2+4}\\right)=\\frac{2}{\\left(x^2+4\\right)^2} \\\\\n& \\text { IF }=e^{\\int \\frac{2 x}{x^2+4} d x} \\\\\n& \\text { IF }=x^2+4 \\\\\n& y \\times\\left(x^2+4\\right)=\\int \\frac{2}{\\left(x^2+4\\right)^2} \\times\\left(x^2+4\\right) \\\\\n& y\\left(x^2+4\\right)=2 \\int \\frac{d x}{x^2+2^2} \\\\\n& y\\left(x^2+4\\right)=\\frac{2}{2} \\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+c \\\\\n& 0=0+c=c=0 \\\\\n& y\\left(x^2+4\\right)=\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right) \\\\\n& y \\text { at } x=2 \\\\\n& y(4+4)=\\tan ^{-1}(1) \\\\\n& y(2)=\\frac{\\pi}{32}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
